lung|PASS: Chest breathing organ is supported and translated as lá phổi for each individual organ. The diagram makes no medical recommendation. Countable singular versus common paired plural is correctly explained, with no unsupported health facts.
reportedly|PASS: The reporting adverb explicitly retains uncertainty; Vietnamese theo nguồn tin does not claim independent confirmation. Fictional missing-statue scenario is original. Grammar distinguishes report attribution from proof of truth rather than using reportedly as an assertion of fact.
statute|PASS: Written law enacted by a lawmaking body distinguishes statute from mere informal rules and from statue. Vietnamese đạo luật is more precise than the source's broad luật lệ. Fictional debate avoids asserting a live legal requirement; countability and under complement are accurate.
warning|PASS: Battery light illustrates a nonverbal sign of possible trouble. Vietnamese báo hiệu rather than a forced lời cảnh báo fits the example. Message/sign definition and warning about/of notes retain the broad source boundary.
carriage|REVIEW: [TRANSLATION] Passenger train and horse-drawn vehicle are separate ordinal boundaries with sensible regional notes. In the horse-vehicle example, Vietnamese nằm cạnh is awkward for a museum display object; replace with được đặt cạnh by overlay, retaining restoration and former owner's photograph.
